WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.040
The machines are here.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.080
Are we going to lose our jobs?

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.520
Will we ever have any 
privacy ever again?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.560
Fiction has long predicted a
radically different world with AI.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.440
And mostly, they're dystopias.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.920
AI's impact used to be
the realm of sci fi.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.560
But then Chat GPT happened
and everything changed.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.960
Chat GPT is being
heralded as a game changer...

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.320
Chat GPT, the artificial intelligence..

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.880
Chat GPT...

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.600
...is this week's sensation

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.640
...is said to be the creator of Chat GPT...

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.560
We're waking up to the threats
from AI pretty quickly.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.040
It's not just the jobs under threat,
the hyper-charged discrimination.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.160
Teachers are sounding the alarm
about the threat to education.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.560
Machine-produced art threatens
to completely alienate us from one another.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:06.120
AI may even pose an
existential threat to mankind.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.160
It's clear that we have to regulate AI.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:08.960
But how?

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:09.840
What should we ban?

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.960
And how can we unleash its
benefits in medicine and industry?

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.570
In this episode of What's Left?, 

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.657
we're going to dive into what we can do

00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:18.456
to make sure that AI helps people

00:01:18.456 --> 00:01:19.600
rather than harms us.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.400
Let's give it a go.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:53.240
What?

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:02.960
Headlines, on AI currently focus on dystopian
concerns about existential threats on AI.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.640
Hypothetical ideas
about it turning on us.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.800
But AI is already hurting people.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.640
Already we see that AI reflects society's
prejudices and structural inequalities.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.720
We've seen AI be racist, be homophobic.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.949
We've seen police use AI to predict crime, 
curtailing basic freedoms

00:02:21.949 --> 00:02:23.680
we had taken for granted.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.080
So what do progressives do about it?

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.120
The EU has to regulate.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:31.420
I spoke to Alex Saliba, vice-president for Digital,

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.160
about what we've done so far.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.840
We also took to the streets
to ask people what they think.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.800
They have to be careful that they
don't overdo it and it stays safe.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.360
You know the film AI?

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.800
I just don't want 
that to happen.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.120
It may be useful, but limited.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.360
We need to see it from a distance.
and for the moment we can't.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.120
When Chat GPT revolutionised
the way that we look at AI,

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.240
when we started seeing the threats 
that AI can pose to our democracies,

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.280
to our privacy, to transparency,
to what is going on online,

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.680
people were becoming much
more aware of the need

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.600
to have a piece of legislation
which basically protects the rights.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.055
The large language models, 
foundation models, generative AI,

00:03:20.055 --> 00:03:25.974
were not part of this regulation initially.
 So we had to modify this legislation

00:03:25.974 --> 00:03:31.017
to adapt to these challenges, 
to have transparency rules

00:03:31.017 --> 00:03:34.388
on deepfakes, on the generation of content

00:03:34.388 --> 00:03:38.080
that needs to be recognised as non-human made.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.760
And also to protect
copyright and authors

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.840
so that they are not depredated by
the training of an AI system

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.280
without their rights being respected.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.640
And we innovated the text
with this because we think

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.080
that this new direction of
AI needs to be regulated

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.960
as much as we did for the
more traditional AI systems.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.122
If you would ask me what changes did you see

00:04:02.122 --> 00:04:04.680
in the discourse a year ago and today?

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:09.088
I would say that people are much 
more aware of the need to regulate

00:04:09.088 --> 00:04:11.600
not only AI, but all digital technologies.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.480
First of all, protecting users,
protecting our consumer rights.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.240
Secondly, protecting privacy rights 
and all the fundamental freedoms.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:24.640
Today we have two worlds: 
The offline world and the online ecosystem,

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.520
and we are interacting heavily
in this online ecosystem.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:32.080
Therefore, we cannot have two
sets of fundamental rights.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:37.000
We, S&amp;D, tried to ban as much
as possible all those techniques

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.840
and the systems that might threaten 
the fundamental rights of people.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.080
Because facial recognition, for instance,
on publicly accessible spaces

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.440
means that you can be targeted,
you can be identified in any moment.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.800
So it affects your privacy life.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.454
You will consider twice before 
going to a protest, for instance,

00:04:53.454 --> 00:04:56.378
because the next day you might lose your job.

00:04:56.378 --> 00:04:58.832
The problem is going to be controlling it

00:04:58.832 --> 00:05:02.320
because it's very easy 
to use it dishonestly and...

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:05.320
then particularly with mass data and...

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:10.480
but that's no different from the Internet and 
they've had a problem controlling that as well.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.720
But it's been of great benefit.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.240
AI will be too.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:15.960
AI is scary.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.760
We cannot just rely on these
Silicon Valley bros to protect us.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:20.880
That's why the EU is doing something.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.480
Some things we just have to ban.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.292
We don't want remote biometric
 identification in real time,

00:05:28.292 --> 00:05:33.567
and in most cases also in non-real time. 
It means the cameras,

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:38.880
to have surveillance on public spaces.
Imagine demonstrations or imagine a protest,

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:45.200
If you are a civil servant and you protest against 
the government, you are not going to do it

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.840
If you know that you can be detected, 
you can be identified in any certain moments.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:53.360
This is always this battle
between freedom and security.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.280
We don't want emotion recognition
in the workplace and in school.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:00.000
We don't want predictive policing.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:04.480
It's just not fair that we violate
the presumption of innocence.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.840
And we have seen that these
systems are simply not working.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:12.760
And in the end, they discriminate people,
especially from certain ethnic backgrounds.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:18.000
We think we need to be very careful about 
all these issues of social control to AI.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.679
With important elections coming up 
in the USA and the EU,

00:06:21.679 --> 00:06:23.840
democracy itself is under threat by AI.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.840
Democracy is a fragile good.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:31.760
It needs to be defended by any
risk of manipulation and control,

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.000
and we need to preserve
the freedoms of our people.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.988
Could you imagine, even in Europe, 
in some places,

00:06:39.988 --> 00:06:46.272
how certain authorities could use these systems 
to create social control against opposition,

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:51.640
against people that are not liked, against minorities? 
So we need to be very, very careful.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.480
That was a lot.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.200
But it's not all bad news.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.560
AI has the power to change 
a lot of things for the better.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:05.120
The impact on medicine, on industry,
is potentially mindblowing.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:08.640
AI is also creating a lot of opportunities,
 new job opportunities,

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:13.000
New opportunities when it comes 
to education, when it comes to research,

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.240
When it comes to the transportation sector.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.760
Therefore, the opportunities are there.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:23.880
What we want to do is continue to enhance 
those opportunities by creating a safe ecosystem.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.320
We should also have more AI literacy.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:34.400
It is useless to have AI and people
not able to use it and enhance its potential.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:38.440
People will have to learn, even though
it's artificial intelligence and robots

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:43.280
we will have to drive the robots initially, 
so people will have to learn artificial intelligence

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.462
and that will lead to more

00:07:44.462 --> 00:07:46.600
artificial intelligence jobs in the market.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:55.480
AI for sure will be able to change our lives
for the better if we manage to regulate it correctly.

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:56.880
It's really a big power.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:03.840
It can really change the way we work, the way 
we do things in a way that can reduce burdens,

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:10.520
can increase our abilities,
can make our time better spent.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:19.000
These advantages, which in general 
we can say are linked to reducing time loss

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:25.640
and also increasing productivity and maybe
give us more free time and have a better life.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:31.160
This is the EU AI Act and we packed it
full of progressive stuff.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:49.000
One of everyone's biggest concerns
is losing their job to AI.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:54.760
Or we are worried about our jobs becoming worse,
more precarious, as we learn to fear our AI managers.

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:59.240
But we've made sure that in the EU, companies
will have to consult with trade unions

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.200
when introducing AI  to the workplace.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:06.920
I think that we should definitely think about
what our economies are actually made up

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.000
in terms of the labour force and
see what we want to protect.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:15.480
So I think it's a really good time for us
to think about what we want as societies.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:21.640
We added in this regulation a reference 
to the need for social dialogue

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:30.120
in view of an agreement to allow us to put
into force an AI system inside the workplace.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.640
We want this to be part
of the social dialogue.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:37.173
Ultimately, if you open 
a small window, especially

00:09:37.173 --> 00:09:43.909
if you open a small window for big tech companies, 
for companies who are thriving on our data,

00:09:43.909 --> 00:09:46.560
who are monetising our personal data,

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.960
then you will have total chaos out there.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:53.430
Therefore, for us, this is always a priority for

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:56.871
safeguarding user rights, 
for safeguarding our privacy,

00:09:56.871 --> 00:09:59.330
for safeguarding fundamental rights online

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:03.030
in each and every piece of 
legislation that we are negotiating,

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.492
that we are moving forward 
here in the European Parliament.

00:10:06.492 --> 00:10:12.090
The S&amp;D put the person in the centre of this 
piece of legislation, while the EPP of course,

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:16.735
they're supporting business, so 
business as usual. And for me, sometimes,

00:10:16.735 --> 00:10:20.680
they really do not care that much 
about the fundamental rights.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:26.680
The Socialists and Democrats Group is working to
make sure that AI is for the many and not for the few.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.320
That it is creating
opportunities for everyone,

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:36.800
that it is creating a better life, a happier life
for everyone and making a better society.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.160
AI is here.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.640
The digital transformation is upon us.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.040
And it's up to us to build
the world we want.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:47.400
To use AI to give power to the people 
and not to curtail our freedoms.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:52.000
AI should liberate people at work and 
not make employment more precarious.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.120
The EU is regulating
with the EU AI Act,

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:59.720
and we're making sure that Socialists and Democrats
are leading the way in writing this.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.280
And if AI does end up winning,
then personally I love AI.

